      "updated_at": "2026-06-05T18:02:39Z",
      "body": "Hello @Tona8941, thanks for the detailed single-GPU vs TP repro and loss plot.\n\nThe important thing to verify here is the vocab-parallel padding path. Megatron normally pads vocabulary size so vocab-parallel logits can be split safely across tensor-parallel ranks; when the requested vocab size is not divisible by TP, loss parity depends on the padded vocab behavior and on whether the extra padded logits/tokens are masked consistently. The existing bot note points in that direction, but we should have a maintainer confirm whether this is expected, a missing warning, or a real uneven-vocab correctness bug.\n\nI am routing this to the tensor-parallel/core owner to confirm the intended behavior and whether we need a warning or test for non-divisible vocab sizes.",
